content.text:
We can use playwright-cli. Later.

Now modify index.html. We need carefully edit strings with minified CSS.

Let's formulate changes.

1. HTML:
- HUD scrap footer `<div class="bar-foot"><span>MARKET</span><span>1.2 / MI</span></div>` → `<span>SCAVENGE</span><span>ONLY SOURCE</span>` maybe.
- Crew heading add morale: `<div class="crew-heading"><span>CREW VITALS</span><span id="crewCount">3 / 3 ACTIVE</span></div>` → `<span>CREW VITALS · MORALE <strong id="moraleVal">70</strong></span>` and right `crewCount`. Better layout. CSS strong.
- Dashboard log add feed:
```
<div class="log"><small>ROAD LOG / <span id="logTime">DAY 01</span></small><span id="logText">The engine coughs to life. Keep moving.</span><div class="log-feed" id="logFeed" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
```
- Market footer tip update and add condition legend. Market parts heading maybe includes legend:
```
<div class="market-parts-heading">VEHICLE PARTS / EQUIP ON PURCHASE</div>
<div class="condition-legend" id="conditionLegend">...</div>
<div class="market-trades parts" id="marketParts"></div>
```
Add `<div class="condition-legend">CONDITION TIERS · <span class="cond rusted">RUSTED +5%</span> ...</div>`. Could make dynamic current condition. Use `id=marketCondition`.
Maybe:
```
<div class="market-parts-heading">VEHICLE PARTS / EQUIP ON PURCHASE</div>
<div class="condition-legend" id="marketCondition">STOCK CONDITION: WORN (+12% EFFECT)</div>
```
And static tier legend in event tip: "RUSTED <25 MI · WORN 25–49 MI · PRISTINE 50+ MI". Nice.
- Maybe road log initial add? Not necessary.

2. CSS add:
```
.crew-heading strong{color:#f0d47a;font-size:9px;margin-left:3px}
.log-feed{display:grid;gap:2px;margin-top:7px;padding-top:6px;border-top:1px dashed #333d38;max-height:58px;overflow:hidden}
.log-line{font-size:8px;line-height:1.45;color:#9fa28d;display:grid;grid-template-columns:8px 1fr;gap:4px}
.log-line:before{content:'›';color:#6f907f}
.log-line.relief{color:#b8c9a2}.log-line.relief:before{content:'☼';color:#a4d47b}
.log-line.tension{color:#d3a58d}.log-line.tension:before{content:'⚡';color:#e69b6d}
.log-line.strain{color:#d6a87e}.log-line.strain:before{content:'⚠';color:#e4ad67}
.condition-legend{font-size:7px;letter-spacing:.6px;color:#8fae9f;margin:-2px 0 8px;padding:6px 8px;border-left:2px solid #45c9c4;background:#12201f;line-height:1.5}
.condition-legend strong{color:#8cf3e7;font-weight:500}
.condition-legend .tier-rusted{color:#c98d6d}.condition-legend .tier-worn{color:#d9c07d}.condition-legend .tier-pristine{color:#8cf3e7}
.part-cond{display:inline-block;padding:1px 3px;margin-right:3px;font-size:7px;letter-spacing:.4px;border:1px solid}
.part-cond.rusted{color:#e0a27d;border-color:#7c5140;background:#2d211c}
.part-cond.worn{color:#edcf86;border-color:#7c6b3f;background:#2c281b}
.part-cond.pristine{color:#a9fff2;border-color:#3f827b;background:#172b29}
```
Need `.rig-slot` content maybe long. Condition prefix adds text; rig slots min-width 33% may overflow. Could format as `<span class="part-cond ...">R</span>`? Requirement prefix. Use full word in rig? Might be long. In rig slot use `part.condition.name` + name; font 7. We'll see. Could add `.rig-slot .part-cond{font-size:6px;padding:0 2px}`.

Mobile log feed font 7 maybe. Add in existing media? We can append a new media block.

3. JS state:
- Add `morale=70`.
- Add nextFlavorAt maybe.

4. Condition code after partCatalog:
```
const conditionTiers=[
 {name:'Rusted', min:0, bonus:.05, key:'rusted'},
 {name:'Worn', min:25, bonus:.12, key:'worn'},
 {name:'Pristine', min:50, bonus:.25, key:'pristine'}
];
function conditionForDistance(miles){let tier=conditionTiers[0];for(const candidate of conditionTiers)if(miles>=candidate.min)tier=candidate;return {...tier}}
```
At 25 Worn. The static tier copy "RUSTED <25 · WORN 25–49 · PRISTINE 50+".
- part display helpers:
```
function partLabel(part){return `${part.condition.name} ${part.name}`}
function formatPartShort(part){...}
function partBonus(id){...}
function scaledPart(id,base){return base*(1+partBonus(id))}
```
Place after rig definitions maybe.

Need avoid `partBonus` naming conflict.

5. `hasPart` works.

6. market:
```
function refreshMarket(){
 const condition=conditionForDistance(dist);
 $('marketCondition').innerHTML = `STOCK CONDITION: <strong>${condition.name.toUpperCase()} +${Math.round(condition.bonus*100)}% EFFECT</strong> · RUSTED <25 MI · WORN 25–49 MI · PRISTINE 50+ MI`;
 ...
 $('marketParts').innerHTML=marketStock.map(part=>`...<span><span class="part-cond ${part.condition.key}">${part.condition.name.toUpperCase()}</span>${part.name} · ${part.slot}<small>+${...}% CONDITION · ${formatPartShort(part)}</small></span>...`)
}
```
Careful the part name is already prefix. Could `part.condition.name + ' ' + part.name`.
- `showMarket`: `const condition=conditionForDistance(dist); marketStock=[...partCatalog].sort(...).slice(0,3).map(part=>({...part, condition:conditionForDistance(dist)}));`
- `nextMarket+=25` at 25 -> 50, at 50 -> 75. Condition at 25 Worn, 50 Pristine, 75 Pristine.
- `$('marketCondition')` exists.

7. `buyPart`: log uses `${part.condition.name} ${part.name}`. `rig[part.slot]=part`.

8. rig rendering:
```
<strong><span class="part-cond ${part.condition.key}">${part.condition.name.toUpperCase()}</span>${part.name}</strong><small>${formatPartShort(part)}</small>
```
Potential width. We'll inspect.

9. Effect functions:
```
function partBonus(id){const part=Object.values(rig).find(p=>p&&p.id===id);return part?part.condition?.bonus||0:0}
function scaledPart(id,base){return base*(1+partBonus(id))}
function hullDamageAmount(...)...
```
Need `hasPart` and `partBonus`.

```
function hullDamageAmount(amount,hazard=false){
 let reduction=hasPart('spiked-ram')?scaledPart('spiked-ram',.30):0;
 if(hazard){if(hasPart('all-terrain'))reduction+=scaledPart('all-terrain',.25);if(hasPart('reinforced-axle'))reduction+=scaledPart('reinforced-axle',.15)}
 return amount*(1-Math.min(.7,reduction))
}
function scrapMultiplier(){return hasPart('salvage-crane')?1+scaledPart('salvage-crane',.25):1}
function rationUseMultiplier(){return 1-Math.min(.5,(hasPart('hydro-interior')?scaledPart('hydro-interior',.20):0)+(hasPart('ration-locker')?scaledPart('ration-locker',.12):0))}
```
- `scrapMultiplier` now 1.25*(1+b), e.g. Pristine 1.5625. good.

Display stats:
```
function formatPartShort(part){
 const b=part.condition?.bonus||0;
 switch(part.id){
  case 'solar-roof': return `+${(0.04*(1+b)).toFixed(3)} FUEL / SEC`;
  case 'spiked-ram': return `−${Math.round(30*(1+b))}% HULL DAMAGE`;
...
  case 'patch-kit': return `+${(1*(1+b)).toFixed(2)} HULL / 20 SEC`;
 }
 return part.short;
}
```
Need unicode minus for consistency.
- For patch: `health += scaledPart('patch-kit',1)`; health fractional; UI rounds.
- solar: `fuel=... + (hasPart('solar-roof')?scaledPart('solar-roof',.04):0)`
- turbo: `const turboSpeed=hasPart('turbo-engine')?1+scaledPart('turbo-engine',.15):1; const miles=dt*1.35*turboSpeed;`
- all-terrain etc use function.

10. tick remove scrap and scavengers:
```
const miles=...
dist+=miles;
const activeCrew=...
const gluttons=...
fuel...
food...
```
Remove `addScrap(miles...)`, `scavengers`.
- Add flavor scheduling:
```
if(elapsed>=nextFlavorAt){pushRoadFlavor();nextFlavorAt=elapsed+rand(4.5,8.5)}
```
- After checkEnd, updateUI. Maybe avoid event + flavor same frame? Fine.
- Add `morale` update in updateUI.

11. Flavor functions before tick:
```
const reliefFlavor=[...]
const tensionPairs=[...]
let nextFlavorAt=6;
function crewByTrait(trait){...}
function addRoadEntry(text,kind){roadFeed.push...; render...}
function pushRoadFlavor(){
 const living=crew.filter(m=>m.health>0);
 if(!living.length)return;
 if(Math.random()<.55){ // relief
   const line=pick(reliefFlavor);
   const gain=Math.random()<.5?1:2;
   morale=Math.min(100,morale+gain);
   addRoadEntry(`${line} MORALE +${gain}.`,'relief');
   $('logText').textContent=line; ? maybe not
 } else {
   // find pair distinct negative
   ...
   const dip=Math.random()<.65?1:2;
   let rationDip=Math.random()<.55?(Math.random()<.5?1:2):0;
   ...
   morale=Math.max(0,morale-dip);
   if(rationDip) food=Math.max(1,food-rationDip);
   addRoadEntry(`${line} −${dip} MORALE${rationDip?` · −${rationDip} RATIONS`:''}.`,'tension');
 }
 updateUI();
}
```
Need avoid `addRoadEntry` using innerHTML with untrusted names? Names static. Fine.

`roadFeed` cap 3. Add first entry maybe after start: "The engine coughs to life..." is logText.

Friction lines generation:
```
const frictionLines = {
 'Paranoid+Reckless': ['{a} watches every mirror. {b} keeps nudging the throttle. The argument dies down, but not before rations are lost.'],
...
}
```
Need pair names inserted. Use `line.replace('{a}',a.name).replace('{b}',b.name)`.
- Pair selection:
```
const negatives = [...new Set(living.map(m=>m.negativeTrait))];
let a,b;
if(negatives.length>=2){
 // pick 2 distinct traits, then members
 const shuffled=[...negatives].sort(()=>Math.random()-.5); ...
} else {
 a=living[0]; b=living[1]||living[0]; // same trait
}
```
Simpler: build all unordered pairs with different negative traits; pick random; fallback first two living.
```
function pickTensionPair(living){
 const pairs=[];
 for(...) if(crew[i].negativeTrait!==crew[j].negativeTrait) pairs.push([crew[i],crew[j]]);
 return pairs.length?pick(pairs):[living[0],living[1]||living[0]];
}
```
Key sorted? Use function find both orderings:
```
const keyA=`${a.negativeTrait}+${b.negativeTrait}`; const keyB=...
const lines=frictionLines[keyA]||frictionLines[keyB]||generic;
```
- Generic friction: `{a} and {b} spend ten miles arguing about {topic}.`
- Topics array.
- Relief lines can include landmark spotting. Some specific:
  - "Eli spots the rusted skeleton of a Ferris wheel on the ridge. The crew stares a little too long."
  - "A clean rain squall washes the ash off the windshield."
  - "Jun finds a working cassette in the glovebox. Nobody asks what happened to the last tape."
  - "Mara coaxes the engine into a smooth rhythm. The cab goes quiet, almost peaceful."
  - "The crew shares a single ration bar in silence. For a moment, the road feels less endless."
  - "A faded billboard promises COLD BEER 12 MILES. Everyone laughs; nobody believes it."
  - "Eli spots a flock of birds heading east. The first living thing in days."
  - "The radio coughs out three bars of an old song before dying again."
- Relief should not restore food, just morale +1/+2.

Tension lines with actual effects:
- `Paranoid+Reckless`: "Mara double-checks the mirror; Eli wants to floor it. Their argument costs ..." Need roles irrelevant. Use names.
- `Paranoid+Glutton`: "{a} rations the food crate while {b} argues for a feast. The fight leaves everyone tense."
- `Glutton+Reckless`: "{a} and {b} split a ration pack to settle a bet. Nobody feels better."
- `Paranoid+Sickly`: "{a} insists on a checkpoint sweep; {b} just wants to sleep. The delay frays nerves."
- `Sickly+Reckless`: "{b} pushes the pace while {a} coughs in the back. The crew snaps at each other."
- `Glutton+Sickly`: "{a} hides an extra ration; {b} notices. The accusation hangs in the cab."
- Specific "Paranoid and Reckless crew member arguing" required: include this exact combo.
- If pair is same trait, generic.

Morale display: heading. Add `moraleVal` to updateUI:
```
$('moraleVal').textContent=Math.round(morale)
```
Maybe color based on morale? optional.

Should road log flavor modify main log? The feed is visible. For accessibility aria-live on logFeed might announce every 5s; okay maybe aria-live polite. Could get noisy but fine.

12. Road events scrap removal:
Let's edit events:
- STRANDED Tinkerer `delta:{scrap:20}` summary `+20 SCRAP / 0 FUEL LOST` → `delta:{fuel:14}` summary `+14 FUEL / SALVAGED PARTS`.
- SCRAP STORM Scavenger `{scrap:20,health:-4}` `+20 SCRAP / −4 HULL` → `{health:10, fuel:6}`? "Strip the roadside metal" → `+10 HULL / +6 FUEL`. Could be too good but okay.
- SCRAP STORM Reckless `{scrap:18,health:-15}` `+18 SCRAP / −15 HULL` → `{fuel:12,health:-15}` `+12 FUEL / −15 HULL`.
- PICKING CLEAN Scavenger `{scrap:20,food:8}` → `{food:20,fuel:8}` `+20 RATIONS / +8 FUEL`.
- PICKING CLEAN Tinkerer `{scrap:24,health:-5}` → `{fuel:20,health:-5}` `+20 FUEL / −5 HULL`.
Any other scrap events? Search.

